<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="012" project="spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>FR-01 server: document-identity resolver extending /api/documents</title>
    <phase>1 Foundation</phase>
    <gate>002 complete — Spike-1 must confirm the `Office.context.document.url` shape for SPE files in Word desktop before this resolver is built</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>New BFF endpoint modifying .cs in `Sprk.Bff.Api`, with authorization, Graph and Dataverse boundaries. Tags include bff-api and auth. Code-review plus adr-check run at Step 9.5.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Architectural: the resolver crosses three seams (Graph behind SpeFileStore per ADR-007, endpoint-filter authorization per ADR-008, Dataverse alternate-key retrieve) and carries a subtle canonicalization rule where ADR-044 applies to the sprk_document GUID but explicitly does NOT apply to the opaque SPE item id. Getting that inverted corrupts lookups silently.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps>002</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, dataverse, graph, auth, endpoint, integration-test, backend</tags>
    <estimated-effort>6-8 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Add a document-identity resolver to the existing `/api/documents` route group that turns an `Office.context.document.url` into the `sprk_document` record it came from, or into a clean "not a Spaarke document" answer. This is the keystone of FR-01: without it the pane cannot know which record and matter the open document belongs to, so version-save, profile display, the record card and open-record are all impossible.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in .NET 10 Minimal API endpoint groups, endpoint-filter authorization, Microsoft Graph shares/driveItem resolution behind the SpeFileStore facade, and Dataverse alternate-key retrieval. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>

  <goal>A route in the `/api/documents` group accepts a document URL, resolves it through base64url encoding to Graph `GET /shares/u!{enc}/driveItem` to obtain `driveId` plus `itemId`, looks up `sprk_document` via the `sprk_graphitemid_uk` alternate key, and returns the resolved document identity (document id, name, related record) — or a clean not-found result for a document that did not originate from Spaarke. Authorization is enforced by an endpoint filter, not middleware. Contract coverage is added by task 016.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      spec.md FR-01 and plan.md §4 Phase 1 task 012. The pane today has no real document identity: `word/WordHostAdapter.getItemId():35-46` returns a fresh `word-doc-{title}-{Date.now()}` string on every call, and `shared/adapters/WordAdapter.getItemId():78-106` hashes title plus author plus creationDate (dead code). Neither identifies a record.
      The `/api/documents` group is created at `Api/FileAccessEndpoints.cs:34` (`app.MapGroup("/api/documents").RequireAuthorization()`). It exposes 9 routes, ALL keyed by `{documentId}`, and every one carries `AddDocumentAuthorizationFilter("read")` or `("share")`. There is NO POST/create route in this group today — this task adds the first route that resolves an identity rather than consuming one, so its authorization shape needs deliberate thought (the caller does not yet know the documentId).
      Dataverse: `sprk_document` carries `sprk_graphitemid` and `sprk_graphdriveid`; the alternate key is `sprk_graphitemid_uk`. Alternate-key retrieve already exists on `IGenericEntityService` (`src/server/shared/Spaarke.Dataverse/IGenericEntityService.cs:26`).
      The canonical resolver to copy (not fork) is `Services/Compose/ComposeRecordResolution.cs:117` `TryFindDocumentByGraphItemIdAsync`, including its column-query fallback at `:254`.
      Gating: Spike-1 (task 002) determines whether `Office.context.document.url` is usable on Word desktop for SPE files. If it comes back negative, FR-01's primary path fails and this task's shape changes (plan.md risk R-1).
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/FileAccessEndpoints.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeRecordResolution.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeCreateOnSavePromoter.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/shared/Spaarke.Dataverse/IGenericEntityService.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Office/OfficeEndpoints.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Office/OfficeService.cs</file>
      <file role="new">projects/spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1/notes/012-identity-resolver-decisions.md</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="002" status="pending">Spike-1 — the confirmed `Office.context.document.url` shape for SPE files in Word desktop. This determines whether the primary Graph path is viable and what the client will actually send.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-007">Scope: every Graph call made by this resolver. Microsoft Graph SDK types MUST stay behind the `SpeFileStore` facade — no `DriveItem`, `GraphServiceClient` or other Graph SDK type may appear in the endpoint signature, the response DTO, or any type that escapes the storage seam. The shares/driveItem resolution belongs behind that facade.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-008">Scope: the new route only. Authorization is an endpoint filter on the route, not global middleware and not an inline check inside the handler. Follow the pattern the sibling routes in `FileAccessEndpoints.cs` already use. Because the caller supplies a URL rather than a documentId, state explicitly in the code comment which filter runs and at what point the resolved document id becomes available for the per-document check.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-044">Scope: the `sprk_document` GUID and every other Dataverse GUID crossing a boundary in this task — canonicalize to bare lowercase via the shared `cleanGuid`. Never interpolate a raw GUID into an OData key predicate. EXPLICIT EXCEPTION: `sprk_graphitemid` is an opaque SPE drive-item id (a STRING, not a GUID) and is matched EXACT-STRING; ADR-044 canonicalization does NOT apply to it. This is verified and recorded at `Services/Compose/ComposeCreateOnSavePromoter.cs:336-339`. Applying GUID canonicalization to the SPE item id would silently break the alternate-key lookup.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: the `sprk_graphitemid_uk` alternate key. MUST NOT be relaxed, widened, or bypassed (NFR-07) — Compose's transient-key dedup and promote-idempotency both rest on it. Read through it; do not add a competing lookup path that tolerates duplicates.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: BFF publish size. Measure the delta against a FRESH BUILD OF MASTER, not the recorded baseline number (root CLAUDE.md §10 bullet 4). Build master in a temporary worktree, publish both, zip BOTH with PowerShell `Compress-Archive` (the method `scripts/Deploy-BffApi.ps1` uses), and report both absolute sizes, the delta, and the zip tool. Escalate at a single-task delta of +5 MB or more; hard stop at 60 MB.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: the PR for this task. State the Placement Justification explicitly per `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md` — why this resolver belongs in the BFF and specifically in the `/api/documents` group rather than `/api/office`. The answer is that it extends existing Graph plus Dataverse plumbing and is latency-coupled to the other document routes; say so and cite the decision criteria.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-010">Scope: DI registrations added by this task. Keep additions minimal; prefer reusing `IGenericEntityService` and the existing `SpeFileStore` registration over introducing a new service registration. If a new registration is unavoidable, justify it in the PR.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-019">Scope: error responses from the new route. Use ProblemDetails for failure shapes. A document that simply is not from Spaarke is NOT an error — it is a successful response carrying "no identity".</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-013">Scope: any AI capability this resolver might reach for. Do not inject `IOpenAiClient` or `IPlaybookService`; go through `Services/Ai/PublicContracts/` if AI is needed at all. This resolver should need none.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Scope: test obligation. A new endpoint requires a contract test. Task 016 owns writing it — coordinate rather than duplicating, but do not consider this task done if 016 has no route to test against. Banned: `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`, DI-registration tests, ctor null-check tests.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Graph shares/driveItem resolution, Dataverse alternate-key retrieve, endpoint-filter authorization</topic>
